{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they shall walk.</b> שחוח, [meaning] bowing down." "<b>And they shall call you the city of YHWH.</b> Now [the phrase] כי קומי אורי refers to Zion." "<b>City.</b> [The construct form] carries over [its construct state] by itself and afterward with its companion [in the full construct chain]. Likewise הוא ציון עיר קדוש ישראל. As in אל באפך תוכיחני (Psalms 6:1)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {1 "The bracketed כי is present in the source text; reading the comment as linking 'city of YHWH' to the address 'Arise, shine' (Isaiah 60:1) spoken of Zion.", 2 "Ibn Ezra argues that עיר in עיר יהוה is grammatically in construct state even though paired with a proper name, drawing analogy to other construct chains including one where אל is in construct before a suffixed form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:32.918627200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}